**1. A method of additively manufacturing a metal part, the method comprising:**  

additively depositing a feedstock comprising metal particles to form a green part having a wall defining a hole extending through at least a portion of the green part;  

positioning a removable support within the hole such that a first ceramic release layer and a second ceramic release layer are disposed between respective portions of the removable support and the wall defining the hole;  

sintering the green part while the removable support is positioned within the hole, the removable support mechanically restraining deformation of the wall during the sintering, and the first and second ceramic release layers inhibiting bonding between the removable support and the wall; and  

after the sintering, removing the removable support from the hole to provide the metal part with the hole having a sintered geometry restrained against distortion during the sintering.

1. A method of manufacturing a metal component, the method comprising:  

   additively manufacturing a metal component body defining an opening;  

   forming, within the opening, a support comprising a metal material having substantially the same composition as a metal material of the metal component body, wherein at least one ceramic release layer is disposed between the support and a surface of the metal component body defining the opening;  

   debinding the metal component body and the support such that the at least one ceramic release layer is converted into loose ceramic powder; and  

   sintering the metal component body and the support concurrently, the support maintaining a shape of the opening during the sintering while remaining separable from the metal component body by virtue of the loose ceramic powder.

1. **A method of reducing distortion of an internal hole in an additively manufactured metal part, the method comprising:**  

   forming a green additively manufactured part having an internal surface defining the internal hole;  

   positioning a metal support within the internal hole, the metal support having an external surface corresponding to a desired geometry of the internal hole and being configured to densify during sintering with a dimensional shrinkage substantially corresponding to a dimensional shrinkage of the green additively manufactured part;  

   providing a first removable ceramic release layer over at least a portion of the internal surface and a second removable ceramic release layer over at least a portion of the external surface, such that the metal support is separated from the green additively manufactured part by the first and second removable ceramic release layers;  

   sintering the green additively manufactured part and the metal support together under a common sintering cycle, thereby co-densifying the green additively manufactured part and the metal support while the metal support supports the internal surface to resist distortion of the internal hole and the removable ceramic release layers inhibit metallurgical bonding between the metal support and the additively manufactured part; and  

   after the sintering, removing the metal support and removing the first and second removable ceramic release layers from the internal hole.
